17 advisory notes — check passed; notes never block dev, test or deploy (most consequential first; check --verbose explains each, snapback4 why <CODE> one):
review — can cost correctness or completeness:
note: schema.q:232:1 — N_NEVER_COMPLETE — review query search: missing pin .conversation; choose the intended scope without dropping other readers (check --verbose) — snapback4 why N_NEVER_COMPLETE
  impact: fine for a screen showing returned rows; proving absence or all matches needs complete: true; keep partial data visible
  audience: completeness is not proved for every caller; runtime complete may still be true (scan messages[..] by read or declaration on messages (at, id) at schema.q:233:10)
note: schema.q:80:7 — N_REFERENCE_UNCHECKED: review: this reference argument has no mandatory target lookup. mutation send stores argument conversation directly in messages.conversation, without a mandatory lookup of conversations[conversation] on every committing path: a reference accepts any well-formed id even when the row is absent — snapback4 why N_REFERENCE_UNCHECKED
note: N_REFERENCE_UNCHECKED (as above) also for mutation add (schema.q:85:3); mutation setLike (schema.q:207:5) — snapback4 why N_REFERENCE_UNCHECKED
note: table followingEdges:1:1 — N_NO_PRODUCTION_WRITER: fix: add a production bootstrap writer. followingEdges: no production writer can bootstrap this root; fixtures and /seed are dev-only — snapback4 why N_NO_PRODUCTION_WRITER
note: N_NO_PRODUCTION_WRITER (as above) also for followingFeed: no production writer can bootstrap this root (table followingFeed:1:1); followingPosts: no production writer can bootstrap this root (table followingPosts:1:1); followingRemovedEvents: no production writer can bootstrap this root (table followingRemovedEvents:1:1); followingWork: no production writer can bootstrap this root (table followingWork:1:1); reposts: no production writer can bootstrap this root (schema.q:170:1) — snapback4 why N_NO_PRODUCTION_WRITER
note: programs.search.0 — N_SEARCH_OPEN: review. opening every membership and head must fit one read; an opening cut refuses E_SEARCH_OPEN without a continuation — snapback4 why N_SEARCH_OPEN
performance — costs speed, meter headroom or offline coverage:
note: schema.q:67:69 — N_SEEK: no action unless it is slow (`check --cost` measures it). a `where` on the next index column is a seek; write it in the key — snapback4 why N_SEEK
note: N_SEEK (as above) also for a (schema.q:72:69) — snapback4 why N_SEEK
note: schema.q:225:1 — N_EPHEMERAL_SERVER: no action unless it is slow (`check --cost` measures it). typingIn runs on the server because it reads an ephemeral table — snapback4 why N_EPHEMERAL_SERVER
note: programs.search.0 — N_SEARCH_WORDS: no action unless it is slow (`check --cost` measures it). word expansion and further-term misses consume the meter; compact membership refills rescan words and charge repeated work — snapback4 why N_SEARCH_WORDS
by design — what a declaration implies; no action needed for online use:
note: schema.q:230:10 — N_SYNC_ORDER: no action for an online app. query searchChat `messages[conversation = conversation] matching q last 20 by .at after c`: the order differs: the page reads by .at, .id, the window by .ordinal, .id; write `last 20 by .ordinal, .id` — it reads messages by .at, .id, newest first (index [conversation, at, id]); its sync window is last 500 by .ordinal, .id, newest first (index byConversationOrdinal [conversation, ordinal]); the client needs the server for this read; offline the ordinary query cannot deliver a complete answer in this order (coverage remains unknown) — snapback4 why N_SYNC_ORDER
note: N_SYNC_ORDER (as above) also for query search (schema.q:233:10) — snapback4 why N_SYNC_ORDER
8 mutations are server-run (online app: no action): compactReceipts (reads receipt-owned or derived field members.deliveredOrdinal), delivered (reads receipt-owned or derived field conversations.lastOrdinal), follow (writes online-only table follows), leave (receipt membership changes and progress need settled state), seen (reads receipt-owned or derived field conversations.lastOrdinal), setTyping (writes online-only table typing), stopTyping (writes online-only table typing), unfollow (writes online-only table follows); 4 mutations have insert arms that may queue; 3 eligible mutations may queue past a horizon — snapback4 why <op>
